{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltied"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTied"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The number attribute is rarely needed to disambiguate ties, since note pitches will usually suffice. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is implied rather than defaulting to 1 as with most elements. It is available for use in more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complex tied notation situations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ties that join two notes of the same pitch together should be represented with a tied element on the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"note with type=“start” and a tied element on the second note with type=“stop”. This can also be done if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two notes being tied are enharmonically equivalent, but have different step values. It is not recommended to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use tied elements to join two notes with enharmonically inequivalent pitches.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ties that indicate that an instrument should be undamped are specified with a single tied element with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type=“let-ring”.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ties that are visually attached to only one note, other than undamped ties, should be specified with two tied","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements on the same note, first type=“start” then type=“stop”. This can be used to represent ties into or out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of repeated sections or codas.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<tied>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The tied element represents the notated tie. The tie element represents the tie sound.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/init(id:kind:number:lineKind:dashLength:spaceLength:position:placement:orientation:bezierX:bezierY:bezierX2:bezierY2:bezierOffset:bezierOffset2:color:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierOffset","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierOffset2","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierX2","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierY","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierY2","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/dashLength","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/kind-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/lineKind","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/number","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/orientation","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/placement","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/position","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/spaceLength"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Enumerations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/document